course: dictionary
lesson: 6634
title: November
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: November is a noun, the name of a month, so it always starts with a capital letter. It is the eleventh month of the year and has 30 days. It comes after October and before December.
explain: Context shows you where November sits. «Halloween, 31 October 2026, is a Saturday, and Bonfire Night, 5 November, is 5 days later, on a Thursday.» The words after October and the day count show that November comes right after it.
explain: The season depends on where you live. In the USA, UK, Canada and Ireland, November is in autumn. In Australia and New Zealand, November is in spring. «Picture a hedgehog curled under a pile of leaves in November» fits the north, where leaves fall in autumn.
fact: November is the eleventh month of the year and has 30 days.
fact: November comes after October and before December.
fact: In the northern half of the world, November is in autumn; in Australia and New Zealand, it is in spring.
fact: The old rhyme «Thirty days hath September, April, June and November» helps you remember which months have 30 days. «Hath» is old English for «has».
exercise: How many days does November have? | 28 | 31 | *30 | 35
exercise: «Halloween, 31 October 2026, is a Saturday, and Bonfire Night, 5 November, is 5 days later.» Which month comes after October? | September | December | *November | August
exercise: Mia lives in Sydney, Australia. What season is November there? | Winter | Autumn | Summer | *Spring
test: Which month is the eleventh month of the year? | December | September | *November | October
test: «A hedgehog curled under a pile of leaves in November» is doing what? | Swimming in the sea | *Sleeping, almost switched off | Singing loudly | Running a race
exam: «From 20 November: November has 30 days, so 10 sleeps take you to 30 November, and 25 more to Christmas.» How many sleeps are there from 20 November to Christmas? | 45 | 30 | 25 | *35
